 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Restaurant Rating Prediction - Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook performs feature engineering on the Dataset.csv file.\n",
    "We will create new features that are expected to improve the model's performance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import necessary libraries\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set random seed for reproducibility\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set plotting style\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8')\n",
    "sns.set_palette(\"husl\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# For better display in notebooks\n",
    "%matplotlib inline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load the dataset\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('../data/Dataset.csv')\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset shape: {df.shape}\")\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Restaurant Name Frequency\n",
    "\n",
    "Restaurants with multiple entries (possibly due to different locations or data entry errors) might have a pattern. We create a feature that counts how many times each restaurant name appears."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Restaurant name frequency\n",
    "restaurant_name_counts = df['Restaurant Name'].value_counts()\n",
    "df['Restaurant Name Frequency'] = df['Restaurant Name'].map(restaurant_name_counts)\n",
    "print(\"Restaurant Name Frequency feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Top 5 most frequent restaurant names:\")\n",
    "print(restaurant_name_counts.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the distribution of restaurant name frequency\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['Restaurant Name Frequency'], bins=20, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Restaurant Name Frequency')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Frequency')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Restaurant Name Frequency\n",
    "print(\"Insight: Restaurants with higher frequency might be chains or have multiple entries, which could indicate consistency in quality or data issues.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Cuisine Popularity Score\n",
    "\n",
    "We hypothesize that restaurants serving popular cuisines might have higher ratings. We compute a score based on how popular each cuisine is in the dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Split cuisines by comma and space, then explode and count\n",
    "cuisines_split = df['Cuisines'].str.split(', ')\n",
    "cuisines_exploded = cuisines_split.explode()\n",
    "cuisine_popularity = cuisines_exploded.value_counts()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Map popularity score to each restaurant based on its cuisines\n",
    "def cuisine_popularity_score(cuisines):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(cuisines):\n",
    "        return 0\n",
    "    cuisine_list = cuisines.split(', ')\n",
    "    # Get popularity for each cuisine, default to 0 if not found\n",
    "    scores = [cuisine_popularity.get(cuisine, 0) for cuisine in cuisine_list]\n",
    "    return np.mean(scores) if scores else 0\n",
    "\n",
    "df['Cuisine Popularity Score'] = df['Cuisines'].apply(cuisine_popularity_score)\n",
    "print(\"Cuisine Popularity Score feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Top 10 cuisines by popularity:\")\n",
    "print(cuisine_popularity.head(10))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the distribution of cuisine popularity score\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['Cuisine Popularity Score'], bins=20, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Cuisine Popularity Score')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Cuisine Popularity Score')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Cuisine Popularity Score\n",
    "print(\"Insight: Restaurants serving popular cuisines may attract more customers and potentially have higher ratings due to established taste preferences.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. City-wise Average Ratings\n",
    "\n",
    "We assume that some cities might have a higher overall rating due to various factors (like income levels, food culture, etc.). We create a feature that is the average rating of the city."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# City-wise average ratings\n",
    "city_avg_rating = df.groupby('City')['Aggregate rating'].mean()\n",
    "df['City Avg Rating'] = df['City'].map(city_avg_rating)\n",
    "print(\"City Avg Rating feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Top 10 cities by average rating:\")\n",
    "print(city_avg_rating.sort_values(ascending=False).head(10))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the distribution of city average rating\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['City Avg Rating'], bins=20, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of City Average Rating')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('City Average Rating')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: City-wise Average Ratings\n",
    "print(\"Insight: This feature captures the local dining culture and standards, which can influence individual restaurant ratings.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Cost Efficiency Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "We create a feature that is the rating per unit cost, indicating the value for money. Higher cost efficiency means better rating per unit cost."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cost efficiency (rating per unit cost)\n",
    "df['Cost Efficiency'] = np.where(\n",
    "    df['Average Cost for two'] > 0,\n",
    "    df['Aggregate rating'] / df['Average Cost for two'],\n    "    0\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"Cost Efficiency feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Descriptive statistics for Cost Efficiency:\")\n",
    "print(df['Cost Efficiency'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the distribution of cost efficiency\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['Cost Efficiency'], bins=20, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Cost Efficiency')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Cost Efficiency (Rating per Unit Cost)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Cost Efficiency\n",
    "print(\"Insight: This feature helps capture the value proposition of a restaurant. Customers often consider both quality and price.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Online Delivery Impact (Binary)\n",
    "\n",
    "Convert the 'Has Online delivery' column to a binary feature (1 for Yes, 0 for No)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Online delivery impact\n",
    "df['Online Delivery'] = df['Has Online delivery'].map({'Yes': 1, 'No': 0})\n",
    "print(\"Online Delivery feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Value counts for Online Delivery:\")\n",
    "print(df['Online Delivery'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize online delivery vs rating\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x='Online Delivery', y='Aggregate rating', data=df)\n",
    "plt.title('Aggregate Rating by Online Delivery Availability')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Online Delivery (0=No, 1=Yes)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Aggregate Rating')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Online Delivery Impact\n",
    "print(\"Insight: Offering online delivery might indicate a restaurant's adaptability to modern trends, potentially attracting more customers.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Table Booking Impact (Binary)\n",
    "\n",
    "Convert the 'Has Table booking' column to a binary feature (1 for Yes, 0 for No)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Table booking impact\n",
    "df['Table Booking'] = df['Has Table booking'].map({'Yes': 1, 'No': 0})\n",
    "print(\"Table Booking feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Value counts for Table Booking:\")\n",
    "print(df['Table Booking'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize table booking vs rating\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x='Table Booking', y='Aggregate rating', data=df)\n",
    "plt.title('Aggregate Rating by Table Booking Availability')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Table Booking (0=No, 1=Yes)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Aggregate Rating')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Table Booking Impact\n",
    "print(\"Insight: Restaurants that accept table bookings might be perceived as more upscale or in higher demand, influencing ratings.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Weighted Rating Features\n",
    "\n",
    "We create a feature that is the product of rating and votes, normalized. This gives more weight to ratings with higher vote counts (more reliable)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Weighted rating (rating * votes)\n",
    "df['Weighted Rating'] = df['Aggregate rating'] * df['Votes']\n",
    "# Normalize by max to keep in similar scale\n",
    "max_weighted = df['Weighted Rating'].max()\n",
    "if max_weighted > 0:\n",
    "    df['Weighted Rating Normalized'] = df['Weighted Rating'] / max_weighted\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    df['Weighted Rating Normalized'] = 0\n",
    "print(\"Weighted Rating and Weighted Rating Normalized features added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Descriptive statistics for Weighted Rating:\")\n",
    "print(df['Weighted Rating'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the distribution of weighted rating\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['Weighted Rating'], bins=20, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Weighted Rating')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Weighted Rating (Rating * Votes)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Weighted Rating\n",
    "print(\"Insight: A rating with many votes is more reliable than one with few votes. This feature captures the confidence in the rating.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Restaurant Service Quality Indicators\n",
    "\n",
    "We combine online delivery and table booking into a service score (0 to 2) indicating the level of service modernization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Service score (online delivery + table booking)\n",
    "df['Service Score'] = df['Online Delivery'] + df['Table Booking']\n",
    "print(\"Service Score feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Value counts for Service Score:\")\n",
    "print(df['Service Score'].value_counts().sort_index())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize service score vs rating\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x='Service Score', y='Aggregate rating', data=df)\n",
    "plt.title('Aggregate Rating by Service Score')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Service Score (0=none, 1=one service, 2=both services)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Aggregate Rating')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Service Score\n",
    "print(\"Insight: Restaurants offering both online delivery and table booking might be seen as more customer-centric and technologically advanced.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Length of Restaurant Name\n",
    "\n",
    "We hypothesize that the length of the restaurant name might correlate with branding or type (e.g., longer names for fine dining)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Length of restaurant name\n",
    "df['Restaurant Name Length'] = df['Restaurant Name'].apply(\n",
    "    lambda x: len(str(x)) if not pd.isna(x) else 0\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"Restaurant Name Length feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Descriptive statistics for Restaurant Name Length:\")\n",
    "print(df['Restaurant Name Length'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the distribution of restaurant name length\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['Restaurant Name Length'], bins=20, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Restaurant Name Length')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Length of Restaurant Name')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Restaurant Name Length\n",
    "print(\"Insight: Longer names might be associated with formal or fine dining establishments, which could influence ratings.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Is Multivariate Cuisine\n",
    "\n",
    "We create a binary feature indicating whether the restaurant serves more than one cuisine type."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Is multivariate cuisine (more than one cuisine)\n",
    "df['Is Multivariate Cuisine'] = df['Cuisines'].apply(\n",
    "    lambda x: 1 if pd.notna(x) and ', ' in str(x) else 0\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"Is Multivariate Cuisine feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Value counts for Is Multivariate Cuisine:\")\n",
    "print(df['Is Multivariate Cuisine'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize multivariate cuisine vs rating\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x='Is Multivariate Cuisine', y='Aggregate rating', data=df)\n",
    "plt.title('Aggregate Rating by Is Multivariate Cuisine')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Is Multivariate Cuisine (0=Single, 1=Multiple)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Aggregate Rating')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Is Multivariate Cuisine\n",
    "print(\"Insight: Restaurants offering multiple cuisines might cater to diverse tastes, potentially attracting more customers.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Log Transformation of Cost\n",
    "\n",
    "We apply a log transformation to the cost feature to reduce skewness, which can help linear models."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Log transformation of cost\n",
    "df['Log Cost'] = np.log1p(df['Average Cost for two'])\n",
    "print(\"Log Cost feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Descriptive statistics for Log Cost:\")\n",
    "print(df['Log Cost'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the distribution of log cost vs original cost\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['Average Cost for two'], bins=20, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Average Cost for Two')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Average Cost for Two')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['Log Cost'], bins=20, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Log Cost')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Log Cost (log1p transformed)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Log Cost\n",
    "print(\"Insight: Log transformation helps in reducing the impact of extreme cost values, making the distribution more normal-like.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Cost Categories\n",
    "\n",
    "We bucketize the cost into categories (Low, Medium, High) based on quantiles for potential use in tree-based models or as a categorical feature."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cost categories based on quantiles\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    df['Cost Category'] = pd.qcut(\n",
    "        df['Average Cost for two'],\n",
    "        q=3,\n    "        labels=['Low', 'Medium', 'High']\n",
    "    )\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Could not create cost categories due to: {e}\")\n",
    "    df['Cost Category'] = 'Unknown'\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Cost Category feature added.\")\n",
    "print(\"Value counts for Cost Category:\")\n",
    "print(df['Cost Category'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize cost category vs rating\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x='Cost Category', y='Aggregate rating', data=df)\n",
    "plt.title('Aggregate Rating by Cost Category')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Cost Category')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Aggregate Rating')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Insight: Cost Category\n",
    "print(\"Insight: Categorizing cost helps in non-linear modeling and can reveal if certain cost segments have systematically different ratings.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary of Engineered Features\n",
    "\n",
    "We have engineered the following features:\n",
    "1. Restaurant Name Frequency\n",
    "2. Cuisine Popularity Score\n",
    "3. City Avg Rating\n",
    "4. Cost Efficiency\n",
    "5. Online Delivery (binary)\n",
    "6. Table Booking (binary)\n",
    "7. Weighted Rating\n",
    "8. Weighted Rating Normalized\n",
    "9. Service Score\n",
    "10. Restaurant Name Length\n",
    "11. Is Multivariate Cuisine\n",
    "12. Log Cost\n",
    "13. Cost Category\n",
    "\n",
    "Each feature is designed to capture a specific aspect of the restaurant that might influence its rating."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "In the next notebook, we will:\n",
    "1. Select features for modeling\n",
    "2. Preprocess the data (handle missing values, encode categoricals, scale features)\n",
    "3. Split the data into training and testing sets\n",
    "4. Train multiple models and evaluate them\n",
    "5. Perform hyperparameter tuning on the best model\n",
    "6. Analyze feature importance and model explainability\n",
    "7. Save the model and preprocessing pipeline for deployment"
   ]
  }
